2026-06-22 22:10:29,713 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-06-22 22:10:29,713 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent answered: To comply with the strict GDPR requirements and other EU regulatory frameworks, our company, Faber IA, already has several security controls in place. We have achieved ISO 27001 certification since 2023, which covers the development, delivery, and operations of our services, including data protection. Our hosting partner, OuraneCloud, provides SecNumCloud compliance at the hosting layer, supporting sovereign hosting of confidential data within the EU.

For data protection, we implement encryption in transit using TLS 1.3 and encryption at rest using AES-256. We also have key management in place through our EU-based infrastructure. Additionally, we use strict partitioning with logical isolation per client and per mission, along with access controls to prevent any cross-client circulation of data. Pseudonymisation is also implemented where relevant.

To ensure reliability and traceability of outputs, our product, Atelier, is grounded in sources and provides retrieval traces and audit logs. It supports internal quality control and statutory audit review, which aligns with the requirement for a complete audit trail and explainability.

Regarding professional secrecy and confidentiality of client data, we are familiar with working under professional secrecy constraints, including those related to GDPR compliance, such as ensuring no transfer of data outside the EU and protecting sensitive data through encryption and pseudonymisation. Our system ensures that all figures and factual statements produced are grounded in and traceable to source documents, with no ungrounded numeric output.

For audit logging and compliance with regulatory requirements like GDPR, we maintain a data processing register, have appointed a DPO, and ensure that our Data Processing Agreement (DPA) is aligned with GDPR Article 28. We also comply with the principle of data minimisation and have configurable retention policies aligned with legal archival obligations.

To address the EU AI Act's requirements, while specific details about the act are not provided in our context, our compliance with GDPR, our use of explainability features in Atelier, and our commitment to transparency in AI decision-making processes help in aligning with broader EU regulations on AI.

In summary, by leveraging our existing security controls, certifications (ISO 27001, ISO 27701 for privacy information management), and compliant hosting infrastructure (SecNumCloud through OuraneCloud), we can ensure compliance with the specified requirements and relevant EU regulatory frameworks.
